Run these lines to get started 

1) Fixes the lidar error that happens upon startup: 
sudo ln -s /dev/ttyUSB0 /dev/rplidar 

2) Start bridge/lidar/gps/UI

./ros2_ws/docker/enter_ros2.sh

ros2 launch robot everything_but_robot.launch.py

Open a new terminal and use this line to pull up UI:
curl http://192.168.8.168:8000/health

user: projectroger
password: bowser

3) Start the robot
Open a new terminal 
./ros2_ws/docker/enter_ros2.sh
ros2 launch robot robot.launch.py
